{% from "macros/forms" import input, textarea as area %}
```

attrs.markdown:
Builds HTML attributes from a hash. It handles the fiddly cases for you:

- null and `false` leave the attribute out;
- `true` writes the name on its own;
- arrays are joined with spaces, skipping empty values;
- everything else is escaped.

---

*page.kiln*

```kiln
<a{{ attrs({
	href: post.url,
	class: ["card", featured ? "card--featured"],
	hidden: false,
	"aria-current": current ? "page",
}) }}>{{ post.title }}</a>
```

*Output*

```html
<a href="/blog/hello/" class="card card--featured">Hello</a>
```
